.SH NAME
sdr2file \- SDR data extraction test program
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBsdr2file\fR \fIconfigFlags\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBsdr2file\fR stress-tests SDR data extraction by retrieving and deleting
all text file lines inserted into a test SDR data store named
"testsdr\fIconfigFlags\fR" by the complementary test program \fBfile2sdr\fR\|(1).
.PP
The operation of \fBsdr2file\fR echoes the cyclical operation of \fBfile2sdr\fR:
each linked list created by \fBfile2sdr\fR is used to create in the current
working directory a copy of \fBfile2sdr\fR's original source text file.
The name of each file written by \fBsdr2file\fR is file_copy_\fIcycleNbr\fR,
where \fIcycleNbr\fR identifies the linked list from which the file's text
lines were obtained.
.PP
\&\fBsdr2file\fR may catch up with the data ingestion activity of \fBfile2sdr\fR,
in which case it blocks (taking the \fBfile2sdr\fR test semaphore) until
the linked list it is currently draining is no longer empty.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.IX Header "EXIT STATUS"
.IP """0""" 4
.IX Item """0"""
\&\fBsdr2file\fR has terminated.
